node_modules/
# package-lock.json IS committed — this is a deployed application, not a published library,
# and the box installs with `npm ci`. Ignoring it meant the deployed dependency tree was
# whatever the deploying laptop happened to resolve, which is how a corrupt @haraka/ocsp
# entry silently broke `npm ci` here and in mta-submit. See README §Deps.
# TLS material is provisioned per-host, never committed.
config/tls/
# Runtime-synced; the committed config/host_list is just the seed/fallback.
config/host_list.synced
*.log
